WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.029
The MCP Inspector: see what the host will see.

2
00:00:03.309 --> 00:00:09.539
The MCP Inspector is the protocol project’s reference tool for testing and debugging servers.

3
00:00:09.819 --> 00:00:18.267
It ships as one npm package with three front ends: a web interface (the default), a scriptable CLI, and a terminal UI.

4
00:00:18.547 --> 00:00:19.592
It needs Node.

5
00:00:19.872 --> 00:00:22.048
js (the docs list 22.

6
00:00:22.328 --> 00:00:23.224
19.

7
00:00:23.504 --> 00:00:28.368
0 or newer) and runs through npx, so nothing is installed permanently.

8
00:00:28.648 --> 00:00:36.755
Point it at the command that launches your server, for example npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector python server.

9
00:00:37.035 --> 00:00:39.296
py, or use mcp dev server.

10
00:00:39.576 --> 00:00:43.032
py from the SDK’s CLI, which opens it for you.

11
00:00:43.312 --> 00:00:46.021
Use the web interface to look, not just to click.

12
00:00:46.301 --> 00:00:51.229
Read every tool’s description and schema exactly as a model will receive them.

13
00:00:51.509 --> 00:00:57.717
Call each tool with good and bad arguments and confirm that bad ones come back as readable tool errors.

14
00:00:57.997 --> 00:01:00.387
Read each resource and render each prompt.

15
00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:06.939
Watch the raw JSON-RPC traffic in the monitoring panel, which shows the protocol era negotiated.

16
00:01:07.219 --> 00:01:10.077
Use the CLI to make those checks repeatable.

17
00:01:10.357 --> 00:01:16.523
A command such as npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector --cli python server.

18
00:01:16.803 --> 00:01:28.685
py --method tools/list prints the tool list as JSON and exits, which fits a CI job that fails when a tool’s description goes missing or a new tool appears unexpectedly.

19
00:01:28.965 --> 00:01:44.517
One caution from the Inspector docs: it stores OAuth tokens and environment secrets in the operating system’s keychain when one exists, and in an unencrypted file under your home directory when one doesn’t (headless machines, many containers).

20
00:01:44.797 --> 00:01:48.275
Know which case you are in before you give it real credentials.
